## Global league 11-10 design (2026-11-11)

The user's 11-10 design (models/NEW-DESIGN.md "The global league"; rule 6 as revised 2026-11-11 ~13:45-13:50) in
leagues/leagues.py. Not launched: no league of this design exists under leagues/, and no recipe rows were added.

- Spec `"models": [{"recipe": "F-L", "ply": 1}, ...]`: each model is a line `<recipe>.p<ply>` that plays at its ply
  only (entries `F-L.p1@<v>-1`, its current version and its champion); the same recipe at two plies is two lines.
  `add LEAGUE --ply P RECIPE...`. No anchors, no ply-1 entries besides ply-1 models', no second-ply entries.
  config.json `"global_design": "11-10"`. Lines have no label: the id shows the ply.
- Champion test at 2 SE, versions G.<major>.<v>, entry as G.0.0 untrained: as before.
- Training (rule 4): each model trains once a cycle, with its own recipe, on the cycle's round-robin games and
  self-games (ordered by round and names) whose players are all rated at or above its current version's Elo minus
  `train.margin` (default 30). "Rated" means in this cycle's fit, as decide saw it. Every entry plays the cycle's
  round-robins before training, so a new entry is rated in its first cycle like the rest. An unrated player
  counts, and a model whose own current version is unrated trains on everything (neither happens in a normal
  cycle). No self-play top-up. cycles.csv keeps train_games, train_positions, train_floor and train_self_games;
  status and the cycle report show them.
- Self-games (on by default): every model entry plays one seeded game against itself a round; never rated. A
  model's set takes an entry's self-games when that entry is rated at or above the model's floor.
- Rule 6, patience by training positions:
  - a cycle without a new champion adds the positions the current version trained on: the training that made it,
    in the cycle before (0 if the line didn't train). Every model accrues, the top one included;
  - 20,000,000 positions (`patience_rule.positions`) retire a model, but not within 5 cycles (`floor_cycles`) of
    its entry or last crowning: crowned or entered in cycle c0, never before c0 + 5;
  - a new champion resets the count to 0. No revivals: add refuses a retired line;
  - the count is exact, in integers: state `patience_total`, `patience_from`, `trained_positions`; cycles.csv
    `patience_positions`, `patience_total`, and `patience` in %;
  - a training log without a position count stops the cycle.
  The percentile rule (11-10 ~21:40) was built first and then removed. patience_cycles is refused for this design.
- Calibration unchanged: 600 own games at depth 1 for every version, ply-2 models included. OPEN CHOICE (for the
  user): a ply-2 model could calibrate on its own ply-2 games instead, at about 10-20x the CPU at P2's prices.
- References random, random-1, random-2, random-3 (random pinned at 0); 5 double round-robins a cycle: the defaults.
- The G option is refused against an 11-10 global league: create refuses it, and try_copy also refuses at run time.
